<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Myos Hormos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Myos Hormos was a port on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, at Quseir al-Qadim north of modern Quseir. Founded under the Ptolemies, it became under Roman rule one of the main harbours for trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, linked by a desert road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coptos">Coptos</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>. The geographer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> reported that some 120 ships a year sailed from it to India.</p></div>
